{"name":"Pioneer Village","hex":"#aa9076","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pioneer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who goes before, as into the wilderness, preparing the way for others to follow.","A person or other entity who is first or among the earliest in any field of inquiry, enterprise, or progress."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be the first to do or achieve (something), preparing the way for others to follow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pioneer"},{"term":"village","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rural habitation of size between a hamlet and a town.","A rural habitation that has a church, but no market."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/village"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fanshawe Pioneer Village","blocks":[{"text":"Fanshawe Pioneer Village is an open-air museum established in 1959 and located in the Fanshawe Conservation Area in London, Ontario. The village uses historical re-enactments to communicate the history of rural communities in the former townships of Westminster, London, North Dorchester, Delaware, West Nissouri and Lobo in Middlesex County from 1820 to 1920 and the founding and development of the City of London up to 1840."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village.jpg/330px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village","wikidata":"Q5434100"},{"title":"Lang Pioneer Village Museum","blocks":[{"text":"Lang Pioneer Village Museum is a living history museum located in the hamlet of Lang in Peterborough County, Ontario. It was established in 1967 by the County of Peterborough. Lang Pioneer Village is situated on the shores of the historic Indian River. Lang Pioneer Village is an \"outdoor museum\" featuring more than 30 restored and furnished buildings, many of which were donated from the surrounding townships. The buildings, constructed between 1820 and 1910, are interpreted by costumed villagers portraying authentic 19th-century pioneer life. Since 2014 the Museum has been the site of the Aabnaabin Encampment, a pre-colonization representation of a Michi Saagiig camp where the story of the First Nations history and culture of the region is told by indigenous interpreters. Lang Pioneer Village Museum is owned and operated by the County of Peterborough."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c8/Lang_Pioneer_Village_Full_Colour_Logo.jpeg/330px-Lang_Pioneer_Village_Full_Colour_Logo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lang_Pioneer_Village_Museum","wikidata":"Q6485609"},{"title":"Pioneer Village (Salem, Massachusetts)","blocks":[{"text":"Pioneer Village, also known as Salem 1630: Pioneer Village, is a living history museum recreating the city of Salem as it was in the 17th century. Opened in June 1930, it was the first museum of its kind in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Kitchen%2C_Governor%27s_Faire_House%2C_The_Pioneers%27_Village%2C_Salem%2C_Mass_%2883010%29.jpg/330px-Kitchen%2C_Governor%27s_Faire_House%2C_The_Pioneers%27_Village%2C_Salem%2C_Mass_%2883010%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pioneer_Village_(Salem%2C_Massachusetts)","wikidata":"Q7196831"},{"title":"Village","blocks":[{"text":"A village is a human settlement or a residential community, larger than a hamlet but smaller than a town; some geographers describe villages as having between 500 and 2,500 inhabitants. Although villages are often located in rural areas, the term urban village is also applied to certain urban neighborhoods. Villages are normally permanent, with fixed dwellings, however, transient villages also exist. Further, the dwellings of a village are fairly close to one another, not scattered broadly over the landscape, as a dispersed settlement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG/330px-Bourton-on-the-Water_2010_PD_09.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Village","wikidata":"Q532"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg/500px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg/1280px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg/500px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Elgie Log House","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFanshawe_Pioneer_Village_log_house.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg/500px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg/1280px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg/500px-Fanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purple Hill Lodge","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFanshawe_Pioneer_Village_Loyal_Orange_Lodge.jpg"},